			<div class="content" id="post-content-3848279">
									

<p>Hawt.<br />
But seriously, I like it, along with the happily ever after :)</p>
<p>It did bring a thought to my head though. If someone makes a new story, well-written and all, cross-linked to this one, where hotaru and knight die grisly deaths&#8230; Would it get downvoted for meta reasons?</p>
<p>I'd like to say I'd downvote it but&#8230; No, if it was entertaining, it'd still get my +1. Sorry, sub-universe. My empathy doesn't extend to fictional characters, even when the fiction assigns those characters non-fictional emotions. You're doomed!</p>
<p>Edit: that's not strictly true, many stories are enjoyable because they trigger our sense of empathy, so I guess it might be more proper to say my morality doesn't extend to them.</p>

